Line-by-Line Slide - typography primitive for HyperFrames.

  Paste the markup and CSS into a composition. Drive the timeline integration
  from a paused GSAP timeline so renders remain deterministic.

  Variables. The script reads each one, falls back to the declared default on
  anything missing or unrecognised, and writes a custom property the CSS above
  consumes. The timeline recipe below is untouched by them: it keeps driving
  one sideways offset, and direction decides which way that offset points.

    - size (compact | standard | display, default standard): type size of the
      stack, 40px, 52px, or 68px.
    - tone (ink | paper | accent, default ink): line colour. ink is near-black
      for light frames, paper near-white for dark ones, accent rides the
      brand token.
    - density (fine | standard | coarse, default standard): the gap between
      lines, 4px, 10px, or 20px.
    - direction (left | right, default left): which side the lines slide in
      from. left keeps the original entry, right mirrors it.

  On every default the result is identical to the original: near-black 52px
  lines, 10px apart, entering from the left.
