Top-Down Letters - typography primitive for HyperFrames.

  Paste the markup, CSS and script into a composition. Drive the timeline
  integration from a paused GSAP timeline so renders remain deterministic.

  Variables. The script reads each one, falls back to the declared default on
  anything missing or unrecognised, and writes the result either into the
  markup or into a custom property the CSS above consumes. The timeline recipe
  below is untouched by them: it keeps driving one offset per letter, and these
  decide which letters fall, how far that offset carries them, and what colour
  they are.

    - text (string, default CASCADE): the word that cascades. Every character
      becomes one span, in source order, exactly like the hand-written markup;
      a space becomes a non-breaking space so it keeps its width in the flex
      row. Anything that is not a non-empty string keeps the shipped word.
    - distance (close | standard | far, default standard): multiplies the drop
      the timeline drives, so the letters cover a shorter or longer run in the
      same time. close covers half of it, standard leaves the shipped 42px
      alone, far carries them nearly double.

